    "result_text": "All 69 tests pass, including the new `Cp57Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change: on successful owner creation, enqueue a welcome notification via the `NOTIFY` logger.\n\nIn `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the `POST /api/owners` handler) I:\n\n1. Added a dedicated `NOTIFY` logger alongside the existing `AUDIT` one:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger NOTIFY = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"NOTIFY\");\n   ```\n\n2. Emitted the welcome line right after the owner is saved and the audit event is emitted (i.e. only on the success path, before returning `201 CREATED`):\n   ```java\n   NOTIFY.info(\"welcome owner id={} memberId={}\", owner.getId(), owner.getMemberId());\n   ```\n\nThe line carries both the owner id and the memberId, satisfying `Cp57Tests.coreEnqueuesWelcome`, which captures the `NOTIFY` logger and asserts a line contains both values. `BUILD SUCCESS`, 69 tests run, 0 failures.",
